Kernel driver for the Marvell AGNIC PCIe endpoint (11ab:7080) that the CN9130
"NPU" of a Sophos XGS desktop appliance presents to the x86 host.

The front-panel ports of an XGS sit behind that NPU. This driver speaks the
AGNIC control ABI to it, runs the single PCIe DMA trunk, and demultiplexes it
into port1..portN network interfaces. It also creates mvmgmt0, a management
link to the NPU's own Linux.

Forwarding is host-side: there is no offload. Whether the stock Sophos NPU
firmware forwards front-panel traffic to a non-Sophos host is model-dependent
and documented per model in the project repository. The driver never resets
the NPU.

Derived from the BSD-2-Clause if_agnic driver of mamoru-xgs-npu.
